<p>An explosive device hit a bus traveling on the Pan-American Highway in Cajibío, Cauca, in southwestern Colombia on April 25, killing at least 13 people and injuring 38, according to regional authorities and multiple news reports; several outlets later raised the death toll to 14 as more information emerged. Officials described the blast as an attack on civilians along one of Colombia’s most important road corridors, and reports said five children were among the injured. Authorities linked the bombing to escalating violence in Cauca, where armed groups remain active despite Colombia’s 2016 peace accord with the FARC guerrillas. President Gustavo Petro and local officials blamed dissident FARC factions operating in the area, while military leaders called the bombing a terrorist act and regional authorities urged stronger action from the central government amid a broader wave of attacks on infrastructure and transport routes.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Y01adFvOLuUP8jd4kBUsU-h3iZ6k0HM4rCwOADn6eYIvFCSoCxRCbcuh5lkL24DfxZfuLSJo8q4qyyhFqyK6qJgy66A142Ych6-B0hXF2CbiDQw7KNrVG2j5ZZxMD9YS6-Ja3ly8nwBS1e5hM-ACZg3gZzLA9M_J6gV2T4UIAcs9WJlCKPfEaWqNUQZypLFqng' alt='Aftermath of the bombing on the Pan-American Highway in Cauca, Colombia' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Road damage: The explosion blasted a large crater into the El Túnel section of the highway and damaged multiple vehicles beyond the bus itself, disrupting a key transport artery in western Colombia.</li><li>Regional alert: Authorities in southwest Colombia were already on alert after a recent series of attacks on infrastructure in the region, pointing to a worsening local security environment before the bombing.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Octavio Guzmán, Cauca governor: The governor said the explosive device detonated while the bus was traveling on the Pan-American Highway and later called for decisive action from the national government after the attack. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/25/explosion-in-southwest-colombia-kills-at-leat-seven-state-governor-says'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Colombian government: Authorities blamed dissident factions of the former FARC guerrilla movement for the bombing. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/colombia-explosives-attack-kills-13-police-source-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Army leadership: Colombia’s army chief called the bombing a terrorist act as authorities tied the violence to worsening insecurity linked to drug trafficking in Cauca. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3351446/explosive-device-kills-13-and-injures-38-bus-colombia'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3351446/explosive-device-kills-13-and-injures-38-bus-colombia'>Explosive device kills 13 and injures 38 on bus in Colombia</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/colombia-explosives-attack-kills-13-police-source-says'>Colombia explosives attack kills 13, police source says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/explosive-device-kills-dozens-on-bus-in-southwestern-colombia-as-violence-persists/article70907596.ece'>Explosive device kills 13, injures 38 on bus in southwestern Colombia as violence persists</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/26/video-colombia-blames-dissident-farc-rebel-for-deadly-bus-bomb'>Video: Colombia blames dissident FARC rebel for deadly bus bomb</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/authorities-in-southwest-colombia-are-on-alert-after-a-spate-of-violent-attacks-on-infrastructure'>Explosive device on a bus kills 7 in southwest Colombia as violent attacks persist</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639070-colombia-roadside-bomb-victims/'>Roadside bomb kills 12 in Colombia (VIDEOS)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href=